Q: LLM throwing error when passed JSON in the prompt A: <p>This error is <strong>not coming from GPT-4.1 itself</strong> — it’s coming from <strong>how the prompt is being passed to the Azure OpenAI SDK / client</strong>.<br />
You are passing a <strong>Python dictionary (JSON object)</strong> directly as a message instead of a <strong>string</strong>.<br />
Azure OpenAI <strong>expects message content to be a string</strong>, not a raw JSON/dict object.</p>
<p>you are passing dict like this one below for example ;</p>
<pre><code>messages = [
    {&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;xyz&quot;, &quot;task&quot;: &quot;summarize&quot;}}
]
</code></pre>
<p>You must <strong>serialize the JSON into a string</strong> before sending it.</p>
<h3>Option 1: Convert JSON → string</h3>
<pre><code>import json

payload = {
    &quot;name&quot;: &quot;xyz&quot;,
    &quot;task&quot;: &quot;summarize&quot;,
    &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Azure OpenAI is powerful&quot;
}

messages = [
    {
        &quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;,
        &quot;content&quot;: json.dumps(payload)  # &lt;-- MUST be string
    }
]
</code></pre>
<hr />
<h2>Option 2: Embed JSON inside text prompt</h2>
<pre><code>messages = [
    {
        &quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;,
        &quot;content&quot;: &quot;&quot;&quot;
You are given the following JSON input:
{
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;xyz&quot;,
  &quot;task&quot;: &quot;summarize&quot;,
  &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Azure OpenAI is powerful&quot;
}

Return the output in JSON format.
&quot;&quot;&quot;
    }
]
</code></pre>
